  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "application (of ointment, cream, paint, etc.); spreading on a surface",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "application (of ointment, cream, paint, etc.); spreading on a surface",
      "explanation": "The act of applying a substance (typically medicine, ointment, or cream) to a surface, especially skin. A formal or technical term commonly found in medical instructions and pharmaceutical labeling."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "24594_tofu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{薬|くすり}を{患部|かんぶ}に{塗布|とふ}する。",
      "english": "Apply the medicine to the affected area.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "24594_tofu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{一日|いちにち}{三回|さんかい}、{軟膏|なんこう}を{塗布|とふ}してください。",
      "english": "Please apply the ointment three times a day.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "24594_tofu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{日焼|ひや}け{止|ど}めは{外出|がいしゅつ}の{三十分前|さんじゅっぷんまえ}に{塗布|とふ}するのが{効果的|こうかてき}です。",
      "english": "Applying sunscreen thirty minutes before going out is most effective.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A formal term for applying or spreading a substance onto a surface, most commonly used in medical and pharmaceutical contexts. In everyday speech, {塗|ぬ}る is the standard verb for applying or spreading.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {薬|くすり}を{塗布|とふ}する: to apply medicine\n- {軟膏|なんこう}を{塗布|とふ}する: to apply ointment\n- {塗布|とふ}{量|りょう}: amount to apply\n- {塗布|とふ}{面|めん}: application surface\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {塗|ぬ}る: to paint, to apply — everyday verb for spreading substances on surfaces\n- {散布|さんぷ}: spraying, scattering — applying a substance by spraying rather than direct contact",
